   "evidence": "RootSetUnion.lean:113-118: the body is `(finite_setOf_natDegree_le_coeff_mem_pi n fun i \u21a6 (s i).finite_toSet).biUnion ...`, so the `Finset` data is used only to produce finiteness proofs.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Card/RootSetUnion.lean",
   "fix": "Change the signature to `{s : Fin (n + 1) \u2192 Set R} (hs : \u2200 i, (s i).Finite)` and make the proof `(finite_setOf_natDegree_le_coeff_mem_pi n hs).biUnion fun _ _ \u21a6 Finset.finite_toSet _`. Update the one caller, `TauCeti/NumberTheory/Height/Counting.lean:116`, to pass `fun i \u21a6 (s i).finite_toSet`. The `ncard_..._pi_le` sibling keeps its `Finset` family because its bound uses `(s i).card`.",
   "issue": "`finite_biUnion_roots_natDegree_le_coeff_mem_pi` still takes `(s : Fin (n + 1) \u2192 Finset R)`, but it only uses finiteness. After this PR its proof just turns each `s i` back into a finite set with `fun i \u21a6 (s i).finite_toSet`. The PR's own reason ('Finiteness needs no computable finset data') applies here too, and Mathlib's `Polynomial.bUnion_roots_finite` likewise takes a finite `Set`.",
   "line": 113
  }
